WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.070
A contract can look PERFECT...

2
00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:04.890
and still be broken inside.

3
00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:07.620
Some are void — they never

4
00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:08.760
existed at all.

5
00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:10.980
Others are voidable.

6
00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:14.480
They stand... until someone sets them

7
00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:15.000
aside.

8
00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:16.890
But here's the catch.

9
00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:19.710
You can only set it aside

10
00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:22.610
if both sides can go BACK

11
00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:23.730
to the start.

12
00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:27.610
You can't put the rock back.

13
00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:29.720
Illegal from the start?

14
00:00:30.310 --> 00:00:33.100
Void. A big mistake you BOTH

15
00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:36.580
made? Void. Your own mistake?

16
00:00:37.310 --> 00:00:40.180
Sorry... you're usually stuck with it.

17
00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:42.590
A lie that gets you to

18
00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:45.750
sign is a misrepresentation.

19
00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:49.130
Innocent... negligent... or fraudulent.

20
00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:55.234
And only negligent or fraudulent gets

21
00:00:55.077 --> 00:00:55.084
you damages.

22
00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:57.840
Small print can't take your rights.

23
00:00:58.610 --> 00:01:01.380
A trader can't exclude injury caused

24
00:01:01.230 --> 00:01:03.940
by negligence. And a ban on

25
00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:04.840
working for rivals?

26
00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:07.040
It has to be reasonable...

27
00:01:07.910 --> 00:01:09.280
or it's VOID.

28
00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:11.650
So — always ask...

29
00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:13.250
does it hold?
